# M3.5.2 local release-gate test diagnostic — 2026-08-27

## Failure

The first complete local M3.5.2 test run passed 14 of 15 cases. The positive
gate case stopped with `TypeError` because `pathlib.Path.stat()` on the active
local Python version does not accept `follow_symlinks=False`.

## Cause and correction

The gate intended to read metadata without following symlinks. `Path.lstat()`
provides the exact portable operation. The implementation was changed only at
that metadata read. No server or runtime action occurred.

## Required validation

The complete M3.5.2 suite and the existing Control restore suite must both pass
after the correction. A partial rerun is not sufficient.
